00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:51.000 line:100%
LU'S SHOP

00:02:07.520 --> 00:02:10.080 line:100%
LU'S SHOP

00:02:15.160 --> 00:02:16.440 line:100%
You're Mr. Lu, right?

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:18.120 line:100%
Yes.

00:02:28.440 --> 00:02:30.800 line:100%
This pair of shoes… I've seen them.

00:02:32.520 --> 00:02:34.600 line:100%
Did someone ask you
to make these this summer?

00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:35.920 line:100%
Who was that person?

00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:37.440 line:100%
No idea.

00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:40.440 line:100%
My dad took that job.

00:02:40.520 --> 00:02:43.080 line:100%
He's out of town getting materials.
Maybe in two days?

00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:54.840 line:100%
Two days later,
that young officer showed up on time.

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:56.320 line:100%
He met my dad.

00:03:05.720 --> 00:03:06.560 line:100%
That's right.

00:03:07.280 --> 00:03:10.160 line:100%
Half a year ago, a young guy came to me.

00:03:10.240 --> 00:03:13.360 line:100%
He insisted I turn
a perfectly good pair of red heels

00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:15.160 line:100%
into blue ones.

00:03:15.240 --> 00:03:18.080 line:100%
It just felt off,
so I didn't want the job.

00:03:19.080 --> 00:03:21.480 line:100%
But then he offered me 800 yuan.

00:03:21.560 --> 00:03:23.160 line:100%
Eight hundred yuan

00:03:23.240 --> 00:03:25.600 line:100%
could buy several pairs
of brand-name shoes.

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:29.040 line:100%
A real pair of shoes,
he wanted it turned fake.

00:03:29.120 --> 00:03:31.280 line:100%
What was he after?

00:03:32.280 --> 00:03:34.280 line:100%
What did he look like? Do you remember?

00:03:36.280 --> 00:03:38.520 line:100%
A guy in his thirties.

00:03:38.600 --> 00:03:39.720 line:100%
Wearing sunglasses.

00:03:39.800 --> 00:03:42.200 line:100%
His face… I didn't see clearly.

00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:44.320 line:100%
How tall?

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:46.240 line:100%
His height…

00:03:47.720 --> 00:03:49.320 line:100%
You, stand up.

00:03:52.840 --> 00:03:53.960 line:100%
About my son's height.

00:03:54.040 --> 00:03:55.400 line:100%
Around 175 cm.

00:03:55.480 --> 00:03:56.800 line:100%
Short haircut.

00:03:56.880 --> 00:03:58.600 line:100%
When he spoke, his voice was hoarse.

00:03:59.240 --> 00:04:01.320 line:100%
He had three burn marks on his arm.

00:04:02.800 --> 00:04:03.640 line:100%
Burn marks?

00:04:03.720 --> 00:04:05.560 line:100%
Scars from being burned with cigarettes.

00:04:11.800 --> 00:04:14.080 line:20%
RAN FANGXU'S PATH

00:04:14.160 --> 00:04:15.520 line:20%
BLUE LEATHER HEELS, LILI

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:17.240 line:20%
DU MINGLIANG'S MOTHER, SHOE SELLER
LIU GUIFANG

00:04:17.319 --> 00:04:22.080 line:20%
SHOEMAKER MR. LU
MAN WITH THREE BURN SCARS

00:04:22.160 --> 00:04:25.920 line:20%
This man is key to solving
the Yuanlongli June 30th case.

00:04:26.640 --> 00:04:28.840 line:100%
Very likely, he's the real killer.

00:04:29.800 --> 00:04:31.280 line:100%
Same plan as always.

00:04:31.360 --> 00:04:32.480 line:100%
We cover both ends.

00:04:32.560 --> 00:04:34.920 line:100%
I'll stay in Yuanlongli.

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:37.520 line:100%
You go to the branch
and check local stations.

00:04:37.600 --> 00:04:40.400 line:100%
Try to find any useful leads.

00:04:40.480 --> 00:04:42.120 line:100%
This is like finding a needle
in a haystack.

00:04:42.200 --> 00:04:45.720 line:100%
If we had fingerprints,
I could search the database.

00:04:45.800 --> 00:04:48.320 line:100%
But those burn scars,
how do I even ask about that?

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:53.880 line:100%
I think Uncle Ran went through
the same thing back then.

00:04:54.480 --> 00:04:57.280 line:100%
Otherwise, he would've caught
that guy already.

00:04:58.600 --> 00:05:00.520 line:100%
Just… think it through again.

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:04.400 line:100%
If you were Uncle Ran,
where would you go next?

00:05:05.560 --> 00:05:07.440 line:20%
RAN FANGXU'S PATH

00:05:20.080 --> 00:05:22.920 line:100%
Han, it's me.

00:05:23.440 --> 00:05:24.280 line:100%
Um…

00:05:26.480 --> 00:05:28.840 line:100%
Hang on! Let me tell you in a second!

00:05:47.240 --> 00:05:48.240 line:100%
My eyes are going blurry.

00:05:48.320 --> 00:05:51.520 line:100%
No idea which idiot came up with this
just to mess with me.

00:05:55.560 --> 00:05:56.520 line:100%
Uncle Ran,

00:05:57.560 --> 00:06:00.120 line:100%
looking at all that stuff,
doesn't it annoy you?

00:06:00.760 --> 00:06:01.600 line:100%
Of course.

00:06:02.280 --> 00:06:04.160 line:100%
It's worse when you can't find clues.

00:06:05.040 --> 00:06:09.600 line:100%
But I have a theory
that helps solve tough problems.

00:06:09.680 --> 00:06:10.480 line:100%
Tell me!

00:06:14.920 --> 00:06:17.320 line:100%
Look, when you're solving a problem,

00:06:17.400 --> 00:06:18.920 line:100%
it's like untangling a ball of thread.

00:06:19.520 --> 00:06:20.960 line:100%
You have to look closely

00:06:21.600 --> 00:06:22.640 line:100%
and find the loose end.

00:06:23.800 --> 00:06:27.000 line:100%
Once you find it, just pull,

00:06:27.840 --> 00:06:30.480 line:100%
and the whole thing unravels.

00:06:31.520 --> 00:06:34.000 line:100%
Right now, I'm looking for that end.

00:06:38.120 --> 00:06:40.080 line:100%
The wind blew it away.

00:06:40.160 --> 00:06:41.960 line:100%
Now it's even harder to find.

00:06:42.040 --> 00:06:44.520 line:100%
That's weird. Why is it so windy today?

00:06:50.040 --> 00:06:51.240 line:100%
Thanks.

00:07:00.400 --> 00:07:02.640 line:100%
PHYSICAL EVIDENCE PHOTOS

00:07:21.480 --> 00:07:24.640 line:100%
LIST OF EVIDENCE

00:07:26.200 --> 00:07:28.840 line:100%
The key to this case… What is it?

00:07:30.720 --> 00:07:31.640 line:100%
WHERE DID YOU HIDE THEM?

00:07:31.720 --> 00:07:32.800 line:100%
I DIDN'T HIDE THEM. SIR, DID YOU CATCH ME
BECAUSE SOMETHING HAPPENED TO MENGMENG?

00:07:35.320 --> 00:07:37.280 line:100%
Why so dumb?

00:07:40.240 --> 00:07:41.200 line:100%
Who are you calling dumb?

00:07:43.760 --> 00:07:45.320 line:100%
Me.

00:07:45.400 --> 00:07:47.320 line:100%
There's been a loose thread here.

00:07:47.400 --> 00:07:49.240 line:100%
How did I miss it?

00:07:49.320 --> 00:07:50.800 line:100%
Q: DID YOU EVER GIFT XU MENG CLOTHING?
A: YES.

00:07:52.160 --> 00:07:54.680 line:100%
Xiaohe, pass me the tape.

00:08:12.760 --> 00:08:15.360 line:20%
PUBLIC SECURITY

00:08:17.120 --> 00:08:18.760 line:20%
WEIYANG PUBLIC SECURITY
BUREAU NANSHAN BRANCH ARCHIVE ROOM

00:08:27.680 --> 00:08:29.000 line:100%
CRIMINAL INVESTIGATION FILES

00:08:33.280 --> 00:08:34.479 line:100%
CRIMINAL INVESTIGATION FILES

00:08:48.600 --> 00:08:50.720 line:100%
Q: DID YOU EVER GIFT XU MENG CLOTHING?
A: YES.

00:08:56.640 --> 00:08:58.200 line:100%
Q: ANY BOWLS DRESS?

00:08:58.280 --> 00:09:00.080 line:100%
A: I MIGHT. I BOUGHT 11 DRESSES
ALL COME WITH DRY CLEANING GIFT CARD

00:09:00.160 --> 00:09:02.920 line:100%
When we interrogated Sun Zhengyong,
I was there too.

00:09:03.440 --> 00:09:05.600 line:100%
Sun Zhengyong had an alibi.

00:09:05.680 --> 00:09:08.080 line:100%
<i>Qu Dahai can also testify for him.</i>

00:09:08.160 --> 00:09:10.080 line:100%
<i>He's not related</i>
<i>to the Yuanlongli June 30th case.</i>

00:09:10.800 --> 00:09:14.440 line:100%
And the Bowls dress
mentioned in the statement,

00:09:14.520 --> 00:09:17.920 line:100%
Xiao Ran already checked the store's
sales records back then.

00:09:18.000 --> 00:09:19.320 line:100%
Everything matched.

00:09:19.400 --> 00:09:21.600 line:100%
<i>Are you sure</i>
<i>this is the loose thread he meant?</i>

00:09:21.680 --> 00:09:24.200 line:100%
I saw Uncle Ran place the tape myself.

00:09:24.760 --> 00:09:26.720 line:100%
Dad, try to think carefully again.

00:09:26.800 --> 00:09:28.960 line:100%
<i>Back then, did Uncle Ran ever mention</i>

00:09:29.040 --> 00:09:31.920 line:100%
<i>the Bowls dress or Sun Zhengyong?</i>

00:09:45.240 --> 00:09:46.360 line:100%
We're back.

00:09:47.800 --> 00:09:50.400 line:100%
BLESSING

00:09:53.440 --> 00:09:55.680 line:100%
You didn't cause Uncle Ran
any trouble, right?

00:09:55.760 --> 00:09:57.400 line:100%
Xiaohe was very well-behaved today.

00:09:57.920 --> 00:10:01.840 line:100%
She even did great
and caught up on all her missed work.

00:10:02.520 --> 00:10:04.400 line:100%
That's all thanks to Uncle Ran.
He taught me well.

00:10:04.480 --> 00:10:05.480 line:100%
Unlike some people,

00:10:05.560 --> 00:10:06.720 line:100%
ask them anything,

00:10:06.800 --> 00:10:08.720 line:100%
they know nothing,
and just shake their head.

00:10:09.440 --> 00:10:11.680 line:100%
Are you taking a jab at me?

00:10:12.520 --> 00:10:14.960 line:100%
I get a question right sometimes, okay?

00:10:15.040 --> 00:10:16.920 line:100%
If teachers taught like Uncle Ran,

00:10:17.000 --> 00:10:18.640 line:100%
using that detective mindset,

00:10:18.720 --> 00:10:19.920 line:100%
I would've graduated early.

00:10:20.760 --> 00:10:24.800 line:100%
You, are you trying to graduate early
to go to Beijing for rock music?

00:10:25.400 --> 00:10:26.800 line:100%
I could even become a cop on the side.

00:10:28.160 --> 00:10:29.880 line:100%
What, on the side?

00:10:29.960 --> 00:10:32.280 line:100%
You, put in the same effort
you use for rock music,

00:10:32.360 --> 00:10:35.280 line:100%
you still wouldn't match
even half of your Uncle Ran's skills.

00:10:35.360 --> 00:10:36.760 line:100%
Uncle Ran isn't a superhero.

00:10:36.840 --> 00:10:38.280 line:100%
He can't even read sheet music.

00:10:40.160 --> 00:10:41.280 line:100%
How about this?

00:10:41.360 --> 00:10:42.800 line:100%
You teach me music notation,

00:10:42.880 --> 00:10:44.000 line:100%
and I teach you criminal investigation.

00:10:44.080 --> 00:10:45.840 line:100%
We learn from each other.

00:10:45.920 --> 00:10:47.040 line:100%
Then who's the teacher?

00:10:47.920 --> 00:10:48.760 line:100%
We both are.

00:10:50.000 --> 00:10:50.960 line:100%
Deal.

00:10:51.760 --> 00:10:53.200 line:100%
Deal.

00:10:53.280 --> 00:10:54.200 line:100%
Rock on.

00:10:55.000 --> 00:10:55.840 line:100%
And even threw up a rock sign?

00:10:55.920 --> 00:10:58.640 line:100%
Hurry and go wash some fruit
for your teacher.

00:11:05.120 --> 00:11:07.640 line:100%
Sir, your package.

00:11:10.000 --> 00:11:11.360 line:20%
QI YUANSHAN

00:11:13.680 --> 00:11:15.120 line:100%
This is the Mount Wu accident file.

00:11:15.720 --> 00:11:16.920 line:100%
We don't need it now.

00:11:17.000 --> 00:11:17.960 line:100%
Perfect timing.

00:11:18.040 --> 00:11:20.120 line:100%
I just wrote something.
Take a look for me.

00:11:23.720 --> 00:11:25.960 line:100%
DEADLY BUILDING CASE
YUANLONGLI JUNE 30TH MEMOIR

00:11:26.680 --> 00:11:28.440 line:100%
This title, it's catchy.

00:11:29.640 --> 00:11:32.040 line:100%
If this gets published,
the title alone will sell it out.

00:11:32.840 --> 00:11:34.800 line:100%
Titles are just for show.

00:11:34.880 --> 00:11:36.120 line:100%
I care more about the content.

00:11:40.440 --> 00:11:42.600 line:100%
ON THE DAY OF JUNE 30TH, 1997…

00:11:45.880 --> 00:11:49.200 line:100%
<i>Times change. Energy's limited.</i>
<i>Focus on the big stuff.</i>

00:11:49.800 --> 00:11:51.360 line:100%
Start with clothes and food.

00:11:51.880 --> 00:11:53.720 line:100%
I get the first three lines.

00:11:53.800 --> 00:11:55.720 line:100%
What does the last one mean?

00:11:55.800 --> 00:11:57.000 line:100%
It's simple.

00:11:57.680 --> 00:11:59.200 line:100%
What can't we live without?

00:11:59.720 --> 00:12:01.200 line:100%
Eating, drinking, and daily needs.

00:12:01.280 --> 00:12:03.280 line:100%
Those things leave clues most easily.

00:12:05.520 --> 00:12:06.560 line:100%
Sir.

00:12:07.440 --> 00:12:08.920 line:100%
That's a great rule.

00:12:09.000 --> 00:12:10.320 line:100%
Why cross it out?

00:12:11.240 --> 00:12:13.440 line:100%
Those were just silly rhymes I made up.

00:12:13.520 --> 00:12:14.600 line:100%
So much for being a top student.

00:12:14.680 --> 00:12:17.200 line:100%
A few words from me fooled you
into calling me "Sir".

00:12:21.760 --> 00:12:23.360 line:100%
Actually, the Yuanlongli June 30th case

00:12:23.440 --> 00:12:25.440 line:100%
has two clothing-related clues.

00:12:26.360 --> 00:12:27.920 line:100%
One is the blue heels.

00:12:29.520 --> 00:12:31.160 line:100%
The other is the Bowls dress.

00:12:33.160 --> 00:12:34.000 line:100%
Right, sir.

00:12:34.600 --> 00:12:36.800 line:100%
Did you write
the Sun Zhengyong interrogation part?

00:12:38.240 --> 00:12:39.200 line:100%
Not yet.

00:12:39.280 --> 00:12:40.680 line:100%
I'm only at Song Qingsong.

00:12:40.760 --> 00:12:42.480 line:100%
Sun Zhengyong, like Song Qingsong,

00:12:42.560 --> 00:12:44.280 line:100%
later ran off
because of illegal fundraising

00:12:44.360 --> 00:12:45.360 line:100%
and debt evasion.

00:12:46.320 --> 00:12:48.920 line:100%
Are you also handling financial cases now?

00:12:49.000 --> 00:12:51.320 line:100%
How did you get to Sun Zhengyong?

00:12:54.280 --> 00:12:57.360 line:100%
Ran did mention Sun Zhengyong to me.

00:12:58.320 --> 00:12:59.640 line:100%
Back then, Uncle Ran

00:12:59.720 --> 00:13:01.560 line:100%
was holding a photo
before he mentioned the loose thread.

00:13:02.440 --> 00:13:06.520 line:100%
<i>But what exactly was in the photo,</i>
<i>I don't know.</i>

00:13:07.560 --> 00:13:08.720 line:100%
A photo.

00:13:09.600 --> 00:13:10.720 line:100%
The loose thread.

00:13:12.360 --> 00:13:13.520 line:100%
Sun Zhengyong.

00:13:17.680 --> 00:13:20.160 line:100%
RAN FANGXU'S PATH

00:13:20.240 --> 00:13:23.240 line:100%
Could it be the dress from Xu Meng's home?

00:13:23.840 --> 00:13:25.320 line:100%
<i>Check it now.</i>

00:13:25.400 --> 00:13:28.000 line:100%
<i>There should be a photo</i>
<i>of a dress in the files.</i>

00:13:28.080 --> 00:13:29.640 line:100%
<i>It's a Bowls dress.</i>

00:13:30.680 --> 00:13:32.600 line:100%
I've gone through
these two boxes a hundred times.

00:13:32.680 --> 00:13:34.560 line:100%
There's no photo of a Bowls dress.

00:13:35.560 --> 00:13:37.640 line:100%
Could it have been borrowed by Uncle Ran,

00:13:37.720 --> 00:13:39.440 line:100%
<i>like those blue heels?</i>

00:13:40.760 --> 00:13:43.760 line:100%
Ran must have compared the photo

00:13:44.480 --> 00:13:46.280 line:100%
and found a problem in the statement.

00:13:46.360 --> 00:13:48.560 line:100%
<i>Go there now. Go to the Bowls store.</i>

00:13:49.160 --> 00:13:51.160 line:100%
Check Sun Zhengyong's purchase records.

00:13:59.680 --> 00:14:00.600 line:100%
Hello.

00:14:00.680 --> 00:14:01.760 line:100%
Hello.

00:14:02.680 --> 00:14:04.600 line:100%
From Nanshan Branch.
I'm here to ask about something.

00:14:05.120 --> 00:14:06.520 line:100%
Ask away, Officer.

00:14:09.240 --> 00:14:10.640 line:100%
You're Jessica too?

00:14:10.720 --> 00:14:12.480 line:100%
When I came five years ago,

00:14:12.560 --> 00:14:14.360 line:100%
there was a male staff member
with the same name.

00:14:15.120 --> 00:14:17.040 line:100%
Here, we change staff, not names.

00:14:19.160 --> 00:14:20.280 line:100%
I wanted to ask.

00:14:21.240 --> 00:14:25.320 line:100%
In 1997, did buying this dress
come with a dry-cleaning card?

00:14:25.400 --> 00:14:26.240 line:100%
Yes.

00:14:26.320 --> 00:14:28.240 line:100%
Not every style did.

00:14:28.320 --> 00:14:30.320 line:100%
But this one is a Bowls classic.

00:14:30.400 --> 00:14:32.160 line:100%
No matter what year you bought it,
it came with one.

00:14:32.240 --> 00:14:34.600 line:100%
And it was a Bowls dry-cleaning card.

00:14:36.000 --> 00:14:37.040 line:100%
Is this it?

00:14:37.800 --> 00:14:38.840 line:100%
That's right. That's the one.

00:14:39.760 --> 00:14:43.080 line:100%
Can you use this card
to find out who bought the dress?

00:14:44.400 --> 00:14:45.480 line:100%
I'm afraid not.

00:14:45.560 --> 00:14:47.480 line:100%
The dry-cleaning cards aren't numbered.

00:14:50.120 --> 00:14:51.240 line:100%
One moment.

00:14:53.920 --> 00:14:56.360 line:100%
This dress was once
brought in for dry cleaning.

00:14:56.440 --> 00:14:59.320 line:100%
Look. Here. There's a check mark.

00:15:01.200 --> 00:15:02.120 line:100%
If it was dry-cleaned,

00:15:02.200 --> 00:15:03.680 line:100%
we can find the record.

00:15:03.760 --> 00:15:05.600 line:100%
I can pull up all the dry-cleaning records

00:15:05.680 --> 00:15:07.920 line:100%
for this dress from 1997.

00:15:08.000 --> 00:15:09.920 line:100%
Dry-cleaning records
are linked to sales records.

00:15:10.520 --> 00:15:12.200 line:100%
-Thank you so much.
-You're welcome.

00:15:15.920 --> 00:15:17.000 line:100%
-Hello.
-Hello.

00:15:17.080 --> 00:15:18.320 line:100%
Excuse me. How can I help you?

00:15:18.400 --> 00:15:20.640 line:100%
I wanted to ask. This store,
how long has it been open?

00:15:21.680 --> 00:15:23.400 line:100%
Our store is the Weiyang flagship store.

00:15:23.480 --> 00:15:24.480 line:100%
It's been open for over 20 years.

00:15:27.120 --> 00:15:30.400 line:100%
Then back in 2003,
did you see this person?

00:15:30.480 --> 00:15:31.600 line:100%
2003?

00:15:32.120 --> 00:15:33.240 line:100%
I was still in high school then.

00:15:36.760 --> 00:15:40.320 line:100%
So, do you have sales records
for the 1997 classic dress?

00:15:40.960 --> 00:15:43.000 line:100%
I'm sorry. Those are internal documents.

00:15:43.080 --> 00:15:44.280 line:100%
We can't just show them.

00:15:45.320 --> 00:15:46.560 line:100%
Police investigation.

00:15:46.640 --> 00:15:48.320 line:100%
It's not that I won't help.

00:15:48.400 --> 00:15:51.400 line:100%
Our store's sales records
are kept for five years at most.

00:15:51.920 --> 00:15:53.880 line:100%
Back in 1997, they were still paper files.

00:15:53.960 --> 00:15:55.240 line:100%
They were destroyed long ago.

00:15:57.440 --> 00:15:59.560 line:100%
But the provincial headquarters
has an archive room.

00:15:59.640 --> 00:16:01.880 line:100%
They should have digital backups.
You can ask there.

00:16:03.240 --> 00:16:04.720 line:100%
Provincial headquarters.

00:16:04.800 --> 00:16:05.920 line:100%
Thank you.

00:16:07.400 --> 00:16:09.440 line:100%
Officer, I'm sorry.

00:16:09.520 --> 00:16:11.480 line:100%
The 1997 records have all been archived.

00:16:11.560 --> 00:16:12.920 line:100%
We need to apply to headquarters.

00:16:13.000 --> 00:16:14.920 line:100%
It'll take about two or three days.

00:16:17.280 --> 00:16:18.120 line:100%
Thanks, that'd be great.

00:16:18.200 --> 00:16:19.560 line:100%
-I'll come back in two days.
-Okay.

00:16:19.640 --> 00:16:21.960 line:100%
HUOFENG INSURANCE

00:16:43.960 --> 00:16:45.000 line:100%
Qiao.

00:16:51.240 --> 00:16:53.120 line:100%
Ran, why did you ask me
to dinner so suddenly?

00:16:53.200 --> 00:16:54.240 line:100%
I wasn't even

00:16:55.320 --> 00:16:56.280 line:100%
prepared.

00:16:57.320 --> 00:16:58.880 line:100%
Why prepare for dinner?

00:16:59.720 --> 00:17:00.760 line:100%
What do you want?

00:17:02.160 --> 00:17:03.440 line:100%
Just some rice noodles is fine.

00:17:06.480 --> 00:17:08.800 line:100%
You ordered braised ribs,
sweet-and-sour fish,

00:17:08.879 --> 00:17:11.840 line:100%
boiled beef, and boiled shrimp,
mushrooms with greens, and egg soup.

00:17:11.919 --> 00:17:13.639 line:100%
Six dishes total.
Would you like anything else?

00:17:13.720 --> 00:17:15.200 line:100%
The shrimp,

00:17:16.280 --> 00:17:17.200 line:100%
maybe skip it.

00:17:17.280 --> 00:17:18.320 line:100%
That's all for now.

00:17:18.399 --> 00:17:20.879 line:100%
-Please serve it quickly.
-Sure.

00:17:23.040 --> 00:17:25.600 line:100%
You ordered too much.
It's expensive and wasteful.

00:17:26.280 --> 00:17:28.440 line:100%
It's fine. We can take leftovers home.

00:17:36.880 --> 00:17:38.680 line:100%
FILE

00:17:40.000 --> 00:17:43.720 line:100%
I pulled this from the evidence room.

00:17:44.560 --> 00:17:46.280 line:100%
After thinking it over,

00:17:47.760 --> 00:17:49.800 line:100%
it's best to leave it with you.

00:18:00.360 --> 00:18:02.160 line:100%
Don't open it yet.

00:18:04.520 --> 00:18:06.960 line:100%
Then, when you tell me to open it,

00:18:07.040 --> 00:18:09.120 line:100%
I'll open it then.

00:18:16.280 --> 00:18:17.640 line:100%
FILE

00:18:27.560 --> 00:18:28.800 line:100%
What's wrong?

00:18:28.880 --> 00:18:31.880 line:100%
On New Year's Eve, what are your plans?

00:18:32.600 --> 00:18:34.080 line:100%
Are you going home?

00:18:37.640 --> 00:18:39.440 line:100%
I don't even have family anymore.

00:18:39.520 --> 00:18:41.120 line:100%
What home is there to go back to?

00:18:41.200 --> 00:18:43.280 line:100%
I'm sorry.

00:18:46.080 --> 00:18:48.560 line:100%
All these years,
I've hated two holidays most.

00:18:49.760 --> 00:18:51.320 line:100%
One is Mid-Autumn Festival,

00:18:52.160 --> 00:18:53.600 line:100%
the other is New Year.

00:19:07.280 --> 00:19:08.160 line:100%
Qiao.

00:19:11.080 --> 00:19:12.160 line:100%
I'm actually

00:19:13.360 --> 00:19:17.840 line:100%
here today to see you
because Sir asked me to.

00:19:19.720 --> 00:19:25.000 line:100%
On New Year's Eve,
he wants to invite you over for dinner.

00:19:26.480 --> 00:19:28.200 line:100%
I'm an outsider. It wouldn't be right.

00:19:28.280 --> 00:19:29.520 line:100%
You guys go ahead and celebrate.

00:19:30.800 --> 00:19:32.520 line:100%
Sir's exact words were,

00:19:33.040 --> 00:19:36.480 line:100%
"Family should have
a reunion dinner together."

00:19:57.640 --> 00:19:59.320 line:100%
If it doesn't work for you,

00:19:59.400 --> 00:20:00.880 line:100%
I I can tell him

00:20:00.960 --> 00:20:02.320 line:100%
-you're going out of town.
-It works for me!

00:20:05.760 --> 00:20:06.760 line:100%
It really is.

00:20:08.440 --> 00:20:12.640 line:100%
But on New Year's Eve,
I promised to take a part-time job.

00:20:12.720 --> 00:20:14.000 line:100%
I might be a little late.

00:20:14.520 --> 00:20:15.840 line:100%
But not too late.

00:20:16.360 --> 00:20:19.080 line:100%
I will come as soon as I'm done.

00:20:21.760 --> 00:20:22.640 line:100%
It's okay.

00:20:23.600 --> 00:20:24.720 line:100%
I'll pick you up then.

00:20:49.360 --> 00:20:50.800 line:100%
BOWLS DRESS

00:20:55.880 --> 00:20:56.720 line:100%
Kiddo,

00:20:57.680 --> 00:20:59.720 line:100%
do you ever get this feeling?

00:20:59.800 --> 00:21:04.400 line:100%
I keep feeling that this Bowls lead,
just like the blue heels,

00:21:05.800 --> 00:21:07.880 line:100%
is a dead end. It goes nowhere.

00:21:07.960 --> 00:21:08.800 line:100%
MAN WITH THREE BURN SCARS

00:21:10.720 --> 00:21:13.600 line:100%
Yuanlongli's demolition is two weeks away.

00:21:14.200 --> 00:21:15.520 line:100%
We need to hurry.

00:21:15.600 --> 00:21:18.360 line:100%
Run the Tremaux algorithm
a few more times.

00:21:18.440 --> 00:21:19.440 line:100%
Again?

00:21:20.240 --> 00:21:22.080 line:100%
You keep running it
on the same few places.

00:21:22.680 --> 00:21:23.640 line:100%
You're just going in circles.

00:21:24.480 --> 00:21:26.640 line:100%
You might as well go to
the provincial capital with me tomorrow.

00:21:27.240 --> 00:21:30.200 line:100%
Whether Bowls is a dead end,
we won't know until we go.

00:21:34.400 --> 00:21:36.080 line:100%
Who messed with this?

00:21:36.160 --> 00:21:37.640 line:100%
Who pulls something like this at night?

00:21:37.720 --> 00:21:39.960 line:100%
Stay away from the window.

00:21:48.280 --> 00:21:50.280 line:100%
Quick, go. Inside, inside.

00:22:04.560 --> 00:22:06.920 line:100%
HOLDOUTS GROUP MESSAGE

00:22:12.880 --> 00:22:16.360 line:100%
Who smashed my window? Was it Qian Dajun?

00:22:16.440 --> 00:22:17.280 line:100%
Get out here!

00:22:17.360 --> 00:22:19.000 line:100%
Is someone going crazy out there?

00:22:20.280 --> 00:22:23.360 line:100%
DU MINGLIANG'S MOTHER
SHOE SELLER, LIU GUIFANG

00:22:42.720 --> 00:22:44.480 line:100%
That Qian Dajun.

00:22:44.560 --> 00:22:47.680 line:100%
Today he smashed a window,
tomorrow he'll break down the door.

00:22:49.480 --> 00:22:50.720 line:100%
I can't go to the provincial capital.

00:22:50.800 --> 00:22:51.880 line:100%
Someone has to stay home.

00:22:52.480 --> 00:22:53.560 line:100%
You go and come back fast tomorrow.

00:22:54.280 --> 00:22:56.000 line:100%
Dad, then promise me.

00:22:56.080 --> 00:22:57.560 line:100%
No matter what happens,

00:22:57.640 --> 00:22:58.920 line:100%
don't get physical.

00:22:59.000 --> 00:23:00.360 line:100%
Call the police if you have to.

00:23:01.600 --> 00:23:04.880 line:100%
With what little they can do,
why would I need the police?

00:23:06.760 --> 00:23:07.920 line:100%
Dad.

00:23:15.080 --> 00:23:17.840 line:100%
Fine. I promise.

00:23:17.920 --> 00:23:19.680 line:100%
If I can argue, I won't fight.

00:23:20.360 --> 00:23:21.240 line:100%
Promise me.

00:23:22.840 --> 00:23:24.720 line:100%
I promise. I promise.

00:23:28.600 --> 00:23:30.920 line:100%
Just don't bother with it today.
Get some sleep.

00:23:31.840 --> 00:23:33.720 line:100%
When I'm back tomorrow, I'll help you.

00:23:39.960 --> 00:23:42.160 line:100%
Be careful going downstairs.

00:24:00.560 --> 00:24:02.680 line:100%
MAN WITH THREE BURN SCARS, BOWLS DRESS

00:24:02.760 --> 00:24:04.760 line:100%
MOTHER OF DU MINGLIANG IN ROOM 1706
SHOEMAKER MR. LU

00:24:04.840 --> 00:24:07.120 line:100%
SONG QINGSONG LIVED IN 1703
OFTEN BROUGHT BACK DIFFERENT GIRLS

00:24:07.200 --> 00:24:09.600 line:100%
RAN FANGXU'S PATH

00:24:35.840 --> 00:24:36.680 line:100%
Hello?

00:24:36.760 --> 00:24:39.320 line:100%
Where are you?
The case briefing is about to start.

00:24:39.400 --> 00:24:41.040 line:100%
-<i>I can't make it back today.</i>
-<i>What?</i>

00:24:41.120 --> 00:24:42.960 line:100%
The case report,
I sent it to Captain Qu last night.

00:24:43.040 --> 00:24:45.120 line:100%
Director Zou wants to praise
you by name at the briefing.

00:24:45.200 --> 00:24:47.800 line:100%
-How can you not be there?
-I'm dealing with something urgent.

00:24:47.880 --> 00:24:49.320 line:100%
I'll ask Captain Zhao
to file my leave request later.

00:24:50.000 --> 00:24:51.600 line:100%
What are you busy with? Why so urgent?

00:24:54.480 --> 00:24:55.640 line:100%
Captain Ran's last wish.

00:25:25.800 --> 00:25:27.560 line:100%
Qiao. Come on.

00:25:27.640 --> 00:25:28.560 line:100%
Have a seat inside.

00:25:39.520 --> 00:25:40.360 line:100%
Uncle He.

00:25:41.520 --> 00:25:42.640 line:100%
I need to apologize to you.

00:25:44.000 --> 00:25:47.440 line:100%
About the demolition,
I did my best to persuade the boss.

00:25:47.520 --> 00:25:49.320 line:100%
But he still sided with Qian Dajun.

00:25:49.400 --> 00:25:52.640 line:100%
He's already given him
full control of the demolition.

00:25:52.720 --> 00:25:56.200 line:100%
Yuanlongli
will likely be demolished early.

00:25:56.280 --> 00:25:57.360 line:100%
I figured.

00:25:57.880 --> 00:25:59.840 line:100%
They started playing dirty last night.

00:26:05.480 --> 00:26:06.320 line:100%
I'm sorry, Uncle He.

00:26:06.400 --> 00:26:08.400 line:100%
Why are you apologizing?

00:26:08.480 --> 00:26:09.480 line:100%
It's not your fault.

00:26:10.640 --> 00:26:12.600 line:100%
It's actually better that you're not
caught in the middle.

00:26:13.600 --> 00:26:15.280 line:100%
Uncle He, please don't do anything rash.

00:26:15.360 --> 00:26:17.800 line:100%
Qian Dajun might do something even worse.

00:26:17.880 --> 00:26:18.880 line:100%
-Who knows what he'll do?
-Let him!

00:26:18.960 --> 00:26:20.680 line:100%
I dare him to try!

00:26:21.440 --> 00:26:22.440 line:100%
Uncle He.

00:26:22.520 --> 00:26:24.640 line:100%
If anything happens to you,

00:26:24.720 --> 00:26:27.320 line:100%
Ran won't be at peace in the afterlife.

00:26:27.920 --> 00:26:29.720 line:100%
To see the Eye of the Vortex,

00:26:30.240 --> 00:26:32.600 line:100%
you must become part
of the Eye of the Vortex.

00:26:35.160 --> 00:26:36.840 line:100%
Those were Ran's words.

00:26:36.920 --> 00:26:38.160 line:100%
None of you understood him.

00:26:39.280 --> 00:26:41.120 line:100%
Only by making up for his regrets

00:26:41.200 --> 00:26:42.840 line:100%
can he find peace.

00:26:50.240 --> 00:26:51.080 line:100%
Uncle He.

00:26:51.160 --> 00:26:56.520 line:100%
Ran gave this to me
just before New Year in 2003.

00:26:56.600 --> 00:26:59.760 line:100%
I don't know
if it can help with what you're doing.

00:27:01.760 --> 00:27:03.240 line:100%
Ran gave you this?

00:27:03.320 --> 00:27:04.160 line:100%
What is it?

00:27:06.880 --> 00:27:08.160 line:100%
I promised Ran

00:27:08.760 --> 00:27:10.480 line:100%
I'd only open it

00:27:11.720 --> 00:27:12.760 line:100%
when he said I could.

00:27:13.360 --> 00:27:16.480 line:100%
But he never got to say it.

00:27:20.920 --> 00:27:22.520 line:100%
SEAL

00:27:37.480 --> 00:27:39.160 line:100%
LIANGLIANG COMPUTER SUPPLIES

00:27:42.840 --> 00:27:44.840 line:100%
What are you doing? Building a bunker?

00:27:44.920 --> 00:27:47.720 line:100%
Uncle He, the surface world has fallen.

00:27:47.800 --> 00:27:49.520 line:100%
Next is our underground world.

00:27:49.600 --> 00:27:51.280 line:100%
I have to arm myself.

00:27:52.680 --> 00:27:53.920 line:100%
Open up and let me in first.

00:27:54.000 --> 00:27:54.920 line:100%
Right.

00:28:07.760 --> 00:28:10.920 line:100%
Uncle He, this drive was formatted.

00:28:11.000 --> 00:28:13.360 line:100%
Everything inside was wiped.
It's all gone.

00:28:15.560 --> 00:28:16.480 line:100%
What do we do?

00:28:17.040 --> 00:28:18.200 line:100%
Can you recover it?

00:28:18.280 --> 00:28:20.520 line:100%
This belonged to Officer Ran.
It's important.

00:28:21.080 --> 00:28:22.120 line:100%
Three minutes.

00:28:27.320 --> 00:28:28.840 line:100%
TOOLS, OPEN DISK

00:28:34.000 --> 00:28:34.840 line:100%
Almost done.

00:28:36.480 --> 00:28:41.040 line:100%
BOWLS INDUSTRIAL CO., LTD.

00:28:44.200 --> 00:28:46.480 line:100%
You must be Officer He, right?

00:28:47.040 --> 00:28:48.280 line:100%
-Hello.
-Hello.

00:28:48.360 --> 00:28:51.640 line:100%
BOWLS INDUSTRIAL CO., LTD.

00:28:53.960 --> 00:28:55.000 line:100%
WEIYANG STORE

00:28:55.080 --> 00:28:56.520 line:100%
1996 to 2005.

00:28:57.520 --> 00:28:59.680 line:100%
The Weiyang store's sales records
are all here.

00:29:02.440 --> 00:29:04.080 line:100%
Officer He, take your time.

00:29:04.160 --> 00:29:05.440 line:100%
I'll make you some tea.

00:29:05.520 --> 00:29:06.960 line:100%
-Thank you.
-No problem.

00:29:11.960 --> 00:29:13.360 line:100%
SALES LOG

00:29:15.440 --> 00:29:19.080 line:100%
SUBJECT SEARCH: SUN ZHENGYONG

00:29:22.800 --> 00:29:23.960 line:100%
DRY CLEANING GIFTCARD REFUND
FOR A SAME DRESS

00:29:30.280 --> 00:29:32.640 line:100%
SUBJECT SEARCH: XU MENG

00:29:32.720 --> 00:29:34.160 line:100%
DRY CLEANING LOG
CLIENT: XU MENG, BUYER: YAO XINCHENG

00:29:34.240 --> 00:29:35.080 line:100%
Found it.

00:29:35.160 --> 00:29:39.040 line:100%
According to the dry-cleaning record,
the buyer linked to this dress

00:29:39.120 --> 00:29:40.320 line:100%
is Yao Xingcheng.

00:29:40.400 --> 00:29:44.160 line:100%
He bought it on December 29, 1996,
at our store.

00:29:44.240 --> 00:29:46.400 line:100%
Yao Xingcheng?

00:29:46.480 --> 00:29:47.400 line:100%
BUYER YAO XINCHENG

00:29:47.480 --> 00:29:50.560 line:100%
RETURN REASON: OTHER REASONS

00:29:50.640 --> 00:29:52.200 line:100%
RETURN DATE: 1997/7/2

00:29:52.280 --> 00:29:53.400 line:100%
That's strange.

00:29:54.080 --> 00:29:54.920 line:100%
What is it?

00:29:55.520 --> 00:30:00.080 line:100%
This Yao Xingcheng's information
only appears in the return record.

00:30:00.160 --> 00:30:02.840 line:100%
His name isn't in the purchase record.

00:30:03.440 --> 00:30:07.320 line:100%
He bought the dress
on December 29 in store.

00:30:07.400 --> 00:30:09.560 line:100%
It was returned on July 2.

00:30:10.160 --> 00:30:11.760 line:100%
The note says, "new returned for old".

00:30:13.080 --> 00:30:14.720 line:100%
What does that mean?

00:30:15.640 --> 00:30:17.800 line:100%
One moment. I'll ask the manager.

00:30:26.760 --> 00:30:27.680 line:100%
Hello, Officer.

00:30:28.200 --> 00:30:29.440 line:100%
I wrote that note.

00:30:29.520 --> 00:30:31.520 line:100%
Back then, this customer
came back after over six months

00:30:31.600 --> 00:30:33.040 line:100%
to make the return.

00:30:33.120 --> 00:30:35.400 line:100%
But the tags and packaging
were all intact.

00:30:35.480 --> 00:30:37.600 line:100%
So the counter canceled the order.

00:30:38.360 --> 00:30:40.160 line:100%
What did the person
who returned it look like?

00:30:40.240 --> 00:30:41.640 line:100%
Do you remember?

00:30:41.720 --> 00:30:42.760 line:100%
I didn't handle the return.

00:30:42.840 --> 00:30:45.840 line:100%
I only found the order while making
that day's report.

00:30:45.920 --> 00:30:49.040 line:100%
This dress had its
button supplier changed in 1997.

00:30:49.120 --> 00:30:52.200 line:100%
This customer bought the old version,
but returned the new one.

00:30:52.800 --> 00:30:53.880 line:100%
I found it strange too.

00:30:53.960 --> 00:30:56.800 line:100%
That's why I wrote that note.

00:30:58.360 --> 00:30:59.920 line:100%
BOWLS FLAGSHIP STORE, SOLD BY SUSAN
COMMENT: WITH ONE DRY CLEANING GIFT CARD

00:31:00.600 --> 00:31:02.200 line:100%
Officer.

00:31:02.280 --> 00:31:05.080 line:100%
The returned dress wasn't bought here.

00:31:05.160 --> 00:31:06.440 line:100%
It was bought
at the provincial flagship store.

00:31:07.640 --> 00:31:08.600 line:100%
What do you mean?

00:31:09.400 --> 00:31:10.680 line:100%
Here's the thing.

00:31:10.760 --> 00:31:14.680 line:100%
This new dress was only distributed
on June 30, 1997.

00:31:14.760 --> 00:31:17.200 line:100%
It arrived at the provincial store
on July 1.

00:31:17.280 --> 00:31:19.760 line:100%
Our Weiyang store is farther away.
It arrived a week later.

00:31:20.280 --> 00:31:21.600 line:100%
So you mean

00:31:21.680 --> 00:31:25.160 line:100%
on July 2, your store wasn't selling
this new style yet?

00:31:25.240 --> 00:31:26.280 line:100%
Right. Look.

00:31:26.360 --> 00:31:28.840 line:100%
On July 2, at 10:05 a.m.,

00:31:28.920 --> 00:31:31.320 line:100%
the provincial flagship store
had a sales record

00:31:31.400 --> 00:31:32.240 line:100%
for the same dress.

00:31:32.320 --> 00:31:34.800 line:100%
But in this record,
there's no customer name.

00:31:34.880 --> 00:31:37.400 line:100%
The return at our store

00:31:38.120 --> 00:31:40.000 line:100%
was at 4:20 p.m. that same day.

00:31:44.080 --> 00:31:45.320 line:100%
Strange.

00:31:45.400 --> 00:31:46.960 line:100%
Bought it in the provincial capital
that morning,

00:31:47.040 --> 00:31:48.480 line:100%
then spent hours rushing to Weiyang,

00:31:48.560 --> 00:31:49.960 line:100%
just to return the dress.

00:31:50.040 --> 00:31:51.560 line:100%
Why go through all that?

00:31:57.600 --> 00:31:59.280 line:100%
This return is strange.

00:31:59.360 --> 00:32:01.360 line:100%
Jessica. Mark it clearly.

00:32:01.440 --> 00:32:04.080 line:100%
In case the customer asks later,
we'll have an explanation.

00:32:04.160 --> 00:32:05.440 line:100%
Yes, Manager.

00:32:10.440 --> 00:32:13.120 line:100%
NOTE: NEW FOR OLD, BOUGHT IN CAPITAL
RETURNED IN WEIYANG. JESSICA

00:32:15.320 --> 00:32:18.360 line:100%
This customer
bought it in the capital that morning,

00:32:18.440 --> 00:32:19.800 line:100%
then returned it in Weiyang
that afternoon.

00:32:19.880 --> 00:32:21.840 line:100%
And it canceled a record
from over six months ago.

00:32:22.640 --> 00:32:23.560 line:100%
Why?

00:32:26.360 --> 00:32:28.320 line:100%
Maybe they wanted to use the return

00:32:28.400 --> 00:32:30.760 line:100%
to erase Yao Xingcheng's purchase record.

00:32:31.480 --> 00:32:34.880 line:100%
Ma'am, can you help me contact
the Jessica who wrote this note?

00:32:34.960 --> 00:32:36.880 line:100%
Jessica from the Weiyang store.

00:32:37.440 --> 00:32:39.600 line:100%
I need to check HR's computer.

00:32:39.680 --> 00:32:40.680 line:100%
One moment.

00:32:40.760 --> 00:32:42.440 line:100%
-Thank you.
-No problem.

00:32:44.200 --> 00:32:46.920 line:100%
Right. Can I make a copy of these files?

00:32:47.480 --> 00:32:49.200 line:100%
Sure. You can copy them yourself.

00:33:06.360 --> 00:33:07.320 line:100%
Uncle Ran,

00:33:09.440 --> 00:33:10.400 line:100%
back then,

00:33:11.200 --> 00:33:12.520 line:100%
did you find this too?

00:33:18.800 --> 00:33:20.480 line:100%
SUBJECT SEARCH: RAN FANGXU

00:33:21.800 --> 00:33:23.000 line:100%
SEARCH

00:33:23.080 --> 00:33:25.080 line:100%
DATE: 2003/1/29, WEIYANG FLAGSHIP
CLIENT: RAN FANGXU

00:33:26.960 --> 00:33:28.560 line:100%
SALESPERSON: JESSICA

00:33:30.760 --> 00:33:32.160 line:100%
STORE: WEIYANG FLAGSHIP
CUSTOMER: RAN FANGXU

00:33:32.240 --> 00:33:33.080 line:100%
<i>Thank you for your cooperation.</i>

00:33:33.920 --> 00:33:34.760 line:100%
Of course.

00:33:34.840 --> 00:33:36.480 line:100%
-I'll get going.
-Okay. Take care.

00:33:36.560 --> 00:33:37.440 line:100%
See him out.

00:33:38.120 --> 00:33:39.280 line:100%
Officer.

00:33:39.360 --> 00:33:40.480 line:100%
New Year is coming soon.

00:33:40.560 --> 00:33:43.040 line:100%
Would you like to see some clothes
and pick one for your family?

00:33:52.200 --> 00:33:53.240 line:100%
Officer.

00:33:53.320 --> 00:33:55.320 line:100%
You're handsome, and you have great taste.

00:33:55.400 --> 00:33:57.040 line:100%
This just came in.
It's the Year of the Goat style.

00:33:57.120 --> 00:33:59.160 line:100%
I can give you an extra discount.

00:34:09.959 --> 00:34:10.920 line:100%
I recovered one file.

00:34:19.400 --> 00:34:20.240 line:100%
Uncle He,

00:34:20.999 --> 00:34:23.320 line:100%
why did Officer Ran save this?

00:34:24.240 --> 00:34:25.560 line:100%
Just close it first.

00:34:26.439 --> 00:34:27.920 line:100%
Right. Eyes off.

00:34:38.479 --> 00:34:39.400 line:100%
He,

00:34:42.640 --> 00:34:44.999 line:100%
this hard drive was probably found
at Wu Shanlong's home.

00:34:45.600 --> 00:34:47.280 line:100%
By procedure, after a case closes,

00:34:47.360 --> 00:34:49.439 line:100%
all assets go to judicial auction.

00:34:50.200 --> 00:34:51.800 line:100%
So this hard drive was wiped.

00:34:52.400 --> 00:34:53.400 line:100%
Looks like

00:34:54.280 --> 00:34:57.520 line:100%
Ran must have bought this hard drive.

00:34:58.720 --> 00:35:00.000 line:100%
I get it.

00:35:00.080 --> 00:35:01.800 line:100%
After this drive was auctioned,

00:35:01.880 --> 00:35:05.040 line:100%
if someone like me knew data recovery,

00:35:06.520 --> 00:35:09.960 line:100%
Officer Ran was afraid the victims
would be hurt again.

00:35:12.120 --> 00:35:13.760 line:100%
That was Ran.

00:35:14.920 --> 00:35:17.000 line:100%
He cared about everyone.

00:35:21.000 --> 00:35:23.120 line:100%
Hello. Please wrap these two for me.

00:35:24.120 --> 00:35:26.520 line:100%
Do you want to wear it now?
I'll take the tag off.

00:35:27.240 --> 00:35:28.360 line:100%
Sure, thanks.

00:35:32.280 --> 00:35:35.240 line:100%
OULI FASHION BOUTIQUE

00:35:35.840 --> 00:35:36.920 line:100%
Welcome.

00:36:01.480 --> 00:36:03.040 line:100%
Do you like this color?

00:36:06.000 --> 00:36:08.640 line:100%
I came to pick a scarf for Sir.

00:36:08.720 --> 00:36:09.600 line:100%
I didn't expect you here.

00:36:13.760 --> 00:36:16.280 line:100%
Which one do you think
would look good on Sir?

00:36:18.440 --> 00:36:19.880 line:100%
No need to bother.

00:36:19.960 --> 00:36:22.520 line:100%
You and Officer He each get one. My treat.

00:36:23.400 --> 00:36:24.440 line:100%
No.

00:36:24.520 --> 00:36:26.400 line:100%
New Year's gift. You can't refuse.

00:36:32.040 --> 00:36:33.120 line:100%
Please wrap them up.

00:36:33.200 --> 00:36:34.080 line:100%
-Sure.
-Thanks.

00:36:34.160 --> 00:36:37.560 line:100%
Sir, I saw your wife
helping you choose for ages.

00:36:37.640 --> 00:36:39.680 line:100%
You two are really close. That's so sweet.

00:36:52.120 --> 00:36:53.440 line:100%
Why did you buy two too?

00:36:55.000 --> 00:36:56.560 line:100%
This one is for Xiaohe.

00:36:57.200 --> 00:36:58.600 line:100%
You got Officer He a gift.

00:36:58.680 --> 00:37:01.120 line:100%
I can't show up empty-handed
and eat for free.

00:37:16.080 --> 00:37:18.640 line:100%
You try it on.

00:37:19.880 --> 00:37:20.800 line:100%
For me?

00:37:23.880 --> 00:37:26.240 line:100%
This, how much was it?

00:37:26.320 --> 00:37:27.920 line:100%
Wool is expensive.

00:37:29.520 --> 00:37:30.880 line:100%
NATIONAL RETAIL PRICE: 1,888 YUAN

00:37:30.960 --> 00:37:32.440 line:100%
This, this is too expensive.

00:37:32.520 --> 00:37:33.960 line:100%
You should return it.

00:37:34.840 --> 00:37:35.720 line:100%
Don't look at the tag price.

00:37:35.800 --> 00:37:38.040 line:100%
I got an extra discount.
It wasn't expensive.

00:37:40.600 --> 00:37:41.480 line:100%
This is a New Year's gift too.

00:37:41.560 --> 00:37:42.560 line:100%
You can't refuse.

00:37:47.720 --> 00:37:51.360 line:100%
You don’t make much every month,
and you still spend like this.

00:37:52.160 --> 00:37:53.720 line:100%
You really don’t know
how to manage your money.

00:38:08.200 --> 00:38:10.520 line:100%
I reached Jessica
from the Weiyang store in 2003.

00:38:10.600 --> 00:38:12.800 line:100%
It matches the clues
Uncle Ran found back then.

00:38:13.960 --> 00:38:16.160 line:100%
We finally caught up with Uncle Ran.

00:38:16.240 --> 00:38:19.040 line:100%
Great. This Yao Xingcheng

00:38:19.120 --> 00:38:21.560 line:100%
is the key to cracking
the Yuanlongli June 30th case.

00:38:21.640 --> 00:38:24.160 line:100%
The Bowls dress at Xu Meng's home
was bought by him.

00:38:24.760 --> 00:38:26.120 line:100%
<i>He didn't want anyone to find out.</i>

00:38:26.640 --> 00:38:29.840 line:100%
<i>So, he used a return</i>
<i>to erase the purchase record.</i>

00:38:30.440 --> 00:38:34.360 line:100%
Also, the man
who went to Mr. Lu to turn red heels

00:38:34.440 --> 00:38:36.200 line:100%
was most likely him too.

00:38:36.280 --> 00:38:37.440 line:100%
<i>Here's the plan.</i>

00:38:37.520 --> 00:38:40.240 line:100%
<i>We keep working both ends.</i>
<i>Once you're back in Weiyang,</i>

00:38:40.320 --> 00:38:41.720 line:100%
go to the bureau first.

00:38:41.800 --> 00:38:43.160 line:100%
Search the internal network.

00:38:43.240 --> 00:38:45.680 line:100%
<i>I'll contact Xu Meng's family now.</i>

00:38:45.760 --> 00:38:48.960 line:100%
We'll try to find this Yao Xingcheng
as soon as possible.

00:38:49.560 --> 00:38:51.040 line:100%
-Okay.
-<i>Talk later.</i>

00:38:54.880 --> 00:38:56.680 line:100%
Auntie Xu.

00:38:57.480 --> 00:38:58.720 line:100%
Xu.

00:39:00.360 --> 00:39:01.720 line:100%
NEW YORK BLOCK

00:39:01.800 --> 00:39:05.440 line:100%
Both corners, put signal blockers on them.

00:39:05.520 --> 00:39:08.320 line:100%
Not one call or text gets out
of this building!

00:39:08.400 --> 00:39:10.520 line:100%
-Got it!
-Okay!

00:39:14.960 --> 00:39:15.920 line:100%
Mr. Qian,

00:39:16.000 --> 00:39:19.320 line:100%
what if the residents run out
and call the police?

00:39:20.480 --> 00:39:21.320 line:100%
Are you stupid?

00:39:22.360 --> 00:39:25.040 line:100%
Cut it off for half an hour,
then turn it back on.

00:39:25.120 --> 00:39:27.840 line:100%
Turn it on, then cut it off.
Cut it off, then turn it on.

00:39:27.920 --> 00:39:28.760 line:20%
AUNTIE XU

00:39:28.840 --> 00:39:29.960 line:20%
Auntie Xu.

00:39:39.520 --> 00:39:42.040 line:100%
NO SERVICE

00:39:45.520 --> 00:39:46.640 line:100%
Qian Dajun!

00:39:46.720 --> 00:39:48.600 line:100%
You shameless piece of trash!

00:40:02.280 --> 00:40:03.200 line:100%
Officer He.

00:40:03.800 --> 00:40:05.040 line:100%
Heading out?

00:40:05.120 --> 00:40:06.280 line:100%
Qian Dajun.

00:40:08.720 --> 00:40:10.800 line:100%
What goes around comes around.

00:40:11.600 --> 00:40:14.040 line:100%
It’s just a matter of time.

00:40:23.840 --> 00:40:24.720 line:100%
See that?

00:40:25.240 --> 00:40:28.200 line:100%
Even that stubborn old man
can't take it anymore.

00:40:29.040 --> 00:40:31.040 line:100%
Those old fools upstairs,

00:40:31.120 --> 00:40:33.320 line:100%
all they’ve got is a big mouth.

00:40:33.400 --> 00:40:35.040 line:100%
Qian Dajun!

00:40:35.120 --> 00:40:36.440 line:100%
You rotten punk!

00:40:36.520 --> 00:40:37.760 line:100%
I'll end you!

00:40:38.280 --> 00:40:39.960 line:100%
Underground garage…

00:40:42.600 --> 00:40:45.160 line:100%
The underground garage
still has a few holdouts.

00:40:45.920 --> 00:40:47.680 line:100%
Especially that Du Mingliang.

00:40:48.280 --> 00:40:50.200 line:100%
Even that little punk dares to act up.

00:40:50.280 --> 00:40:51.640 line:100%
Then we start with him.

00:40:52.480 --> 00:40:54.280 line:100%
Make an example of him.

00:41:02.760 --> 00:41:05.200 line:100%
BLESSING

00:41:23.600 --> 00:41:27.160 line:100%
BLESSING, GOOD FORTUNE

00:41:40.440 --> 00:41:41.560 line:100%
Auntie Xu.

00:41:43.560 --> 00:41:44.720 line:100%
Who is it?

00:41:50.400 --> 00:41:51.920 line:100%
It's me, Auntie Xu.

00:41:58.480 --> 00:41:59.680 line:100%
Officer He?

00:42:02.320 --> 00:42:04.760 line:100%
Officer He, you've gotten old.

00:42:04.840 --> 00:42:07.200 line:100%
Come on, have a seat.
I'll get you some water.

00:42:07.280 --> 00:42:08.240 line:100%
No need.

00:42:08.760 --> 00:42:10.240 line:100%
These are for you.

00:42:10.880 --> 00:42:12.800 line:100%
Thank you.

00:42:12.880 --> 00:42:15.440 line:100%
I'm here to ask about something.

00:42:16.200 --> 00:42:19.280 line:100%
Back then, did Xu Meng and Xu Zhihong

00:42:19.360 --> 00:42:23.520 line:100%
know someone named Yao Xingcheng?

00:42:24.040 --> 00:42:25.480 line:100%
Yao Xingcheng?

00:42:26.920 --> 00:42:29.320 line:100%
Yao Xingcheng.

00:42:30.240 --> 00:42:31.080 line:100%
Yao…

00:42:32.720 --> 00:42:35.360 line:100%
I remember now. I remember.

00:42:35.440 --> 00:42:39.200 line:100%
One year, around New Year,

00:42:39.280 --> 00:42:41.160 line:100%
a young man came by.

00:42:41.240 --> 00:42:44.200 line:100%
He said he was a police officer too.

00:42:44.280 --> 00:42:48.920 line:100%
He asked me about Yao Xingcheng.

00:42:49.000 --> 00:42:53.320 line:100%
But I had never heard that name.

00:42:55.000 --> 00:42:59.280 line:100%
That young man was not only handsome,
but also kind.

00:42:59.800 --> 00:43:03.160 line:100%
When he left, he insisted
on giving me a red envelope.

00:43:03.240 --> 00:43:07.240 line:100%
Officer He, how has he been?

00:43:08.200 --> 00:43:09.600 line:100%
Is he married?

00:43:09.680 --> 00:43:11.480 line:100%
Does he have kids?